  "label": "The cat is mapped as 'me' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'me neither. make some!' explicitly uses the pronoun 'me', which is analogically mapped onto the visual entity of the gray cat. The cat's grumpy, indifferent expression is anthropomorphized to represent the speaker's own emotional state — apathy toward the coffee smell and a demand for action. This creates a direct analogical mapping where the cat visually embodies the textual 'me'.",
